A||N||1||TRL46202||Oil leak! HELP.....||||5||
Z||000000||TRL46202||04-13-2000||09:41 PM||||I have an 87GT, I'm having a oil leak and can't seem to find it. Looking at the front of the engine, right side front corner, I degreased what I could get to. I thought the oil pan was leaking so I tightened the nuts. I drove for a few days and noticed a drop on the driveway. Jacked the car up pulled the pass. rear wheel and took the cover for the wheel well off and noticed that there was oil coming down the antifreeze hose just where it connects to the bottom of the thermostat housing. I tried to shine a light up there but couldn't see much. I then climed on top and reached around the backside to feel along the lip on the valve cover and found a little oil around the bolt just between #2 and #4 plugs, so I was able to tighten that one, 1 1/2 truns, all the rest seemed tight and no oil around the rest of the valve cover. It has me baffled, is there a oil sending unit somewhere in that area,? I know that I've heard about the dis. "O" ring leaking but that would be on the other end? I have heard of this Oil sending unit but the book I have "Haynes" doesn't mention it at all. I do know that there was a new timing chain installed some time ago and a new water pump but the oil doesn't seem to be coming from any of those parts. Any help would be great!<P>Thanks, Tom<BR> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||04-13-2000||10:47 PM||||I would guess that you have a oil sending unit leaking. It Is located on top of the block close to the battery. Also It would make you think It was leaking around number 2 cyl. It is about two Inches in diamater and has a wiring connector on top||||reg||1
